      "summary": "The prior self-witness issue is addressed by requiring a witness from an existing non-response document. The new review path adds a separate persistence step after the response commit, leaving a partial response possible if that step fails.",
      "findingList": [
        {
          "severity": "major",
          "file": "backend/AirlineDemo.Api/Requests/MockResponseEndpoints.cs",
          "line": 107,
          "message": "The response commit and the new review work-item write are not atomic. A failure during reassessment can leave an accepted response persisted even though the operation fails.",
          "confidence": 0.88,
          "category": "logic-error",
          "evidence": {
            "codePathTraced": "When no independent witness exists, the new responseClaims list is empty. AssessmentExecutionService.Assess routes that to Review and calls CaseStateStore.CreateWorkItem, which persists separately after the response basis, receipt, and audit event were committed at line 103.",
            "failureScenario": "If persistence fails during the work-item write, Accept throws after the response is already stored. The caller sees a failure, but the basis, receipt, and audit event remain, violating AC: RESPONSE-02's no-partial-response requirement."
          }
        }
      ]
